{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "Wrote the skid_buffer RTL, its self-checking testbench and a single-task proof setup. The design follows the approved microarchitecture and interface spec. Review is not done yet, and the platform's own lint, simulation, synthesis, formal and cover checks have not run on these files.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "Implementation choices for skid_buffer", "summary": "The RTL follows the next-state table and state in [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.microarchitecture.a1] for the requirement [requirement:req-49d207f970]. It has two registers, m_valid/m_data and skid_valid/skid_data, and s_ready is the inverse of skid_valid. The next state is worked out in an always @* block, and the registers hold only the reset and the load. Only the valid bits are reset (synchronous, active low), as [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.interface-spec.a1] section 5 and the microarchitecture section 2 set out. One addition the spec does not mention: m_data loads s_data only when s_valid is high, so it does not toggle on idle cycles. The spec leaves data undefined while valid is low, so this does not change behaviour at the ports."}], "files": [{"path": "skid_buffer.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "skid_buffer RTL", "summary": "A two-register valid/ready slice built to [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.microarchitecture.a1] and [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.interface-spec.a1]. Every output comes from a flop. The formal properties sit under ifdef FORMAL: a model queue of up to two beats, the hold rule, a check that the skid register holds the newer beat, and covers for stall, a full slice, a drain and full throughput.", "entry": "skid_buffer"}, {"path": "skid_buffer_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking testbench, lanes at WIDTH 8 and 1", "summary": "Checks the slice against a model on every cycle, as set out in the verification plan of [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.microarchitecture.a1] and section 6 of [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.interface-spec.a1]. It covers reset values, latency, a 64-beat stream at full throughput, stalls with one and two beats held, every beat out in order and once, the hold rule, and outputs that must not move within a cycle when m_ready, s_valid or s_data are flipped. It then runs 3000 cycles of random traffic with a drain, and a reset with beats held. Failures are reported with $error, and the run ends with the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line.", "entry": "skid_buffer_tb"}, {"path": "skid_buffer.sby", "kind": "formal_spec", "title": "SymbiYosys proof setup at WIDTH 8", "summary": "One .sby file with no [tasks], mode prove, depth 20, the smtbmc engine, reading skid_buffer.v. It proves the queue properties from [artifact:prj-ba2f05400a.microarchitecture.a1] at the default WIDTH.", "entry": "skid_buffer"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Advisory runs during drafting reported: Verilator lint clean (run-0001), every property proven (run-0002), all 4 covers and all 8 assertion antecedents reached (run-0003), and the Icarus simulation passing 27800 checks with 0 failed (run-0004). These runs are not evidence; the platform's own checks on the final files decide.", "The simulation run used the same RTL without the ifdef FORMAL block. That block is not compiled in simulation."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Two gaps against the spec, both recorded: (1) The platform takes exactly one .sby file, so the proof runs only at WIDTH 8. WIDTH 1 is checked in simulation through the second testbench lane, and the microarchitecture's skid_buffer_w1.sby is not supplied. (2) Synthesis has not been tried in this session. The design has full defaults in its combinational block, so no latch is expected. No mutation (deliberately broken design) test was run. Independent review is still needed."}

=== FILE: skid_buffer.v ===
`default_nettype none
// skid_buffer: two-register valid/ready slice (microarchitecture.md).
module skid_buffer #(
  parameter integer WIDTH = 8
) (
  input  wire             clk,
  input  wire             rst_n,
  input  wire             s_valid,
  output wire             s_ready,
  input  wire [WIDTH-1:0] s_data,
  output reg              m_valid,
  input  wire             m_ready,
  output reg  [WIDTH-1:0] m_data
);

  reg             skid_valid;
  reg [WIDTH-1:0] skid_data;

  reg m_valid_d;
  reg skid_valid_d;
  reg m_load;
  reg m_from_skid;
  reg skid_load;

  wire m_free = !m_valid || m_ready;
  wire s_fire = s_valid && !skid_valid;

  assign s_ready = !skid_valid;

  always @* begin
    m_valid_d    = m_valid;
    skid_valid_d = skid_valid;
    m_load       = 1'b0;
    m_from_skid  = 1'b0;
    skid_load    = 1'b0;
    if (m_free) begin
      if (skid_valid) begin
        m_valid_d    = 1'b1;
        m_load       = 1'b1;
        m_from_skid  = 1'b1;
        skid_valid_d = 1'b0;
      end else begin
        m_valid_d = s_valid;
        m_load    = s_valid;
      end
    end else if (s_fire) begin
      skid_valid_d = 1'b1;
      skid_load    = 1'b1;
    end
  end

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (!rst_n) begin
      m_valid    <= 1'b0;
      skid_valid <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
      m_valid    <= m_valid_d;
      skid_valid <= skid_valid_d;
    end
  end

  // Data registers are not reset (microarchitecture.md section 2).
  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (m_load) begin
      m_data <= m_from_skid ? skid_data : s_data;
    end
    if (skid_load) begin
      skid_data <= s_data;
    end
  end

`ifdef FORMAL
  reg f_past_valid = 1'b0;
  always @(posedge clk) f_past_valid <= 1'b1;
  always @(*) if (!f_past_valid) assume(!rst_n);

  reg [1:0]       f_cnt;
  reg [WIDTH-1:0] f_q0;
  reg [WIDTH-1:0] f_q1;
  reg             f_was_full;
  wire f_in  = s_valid && s_ready;
  wire f_out = m_valid && m_ready;

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (!rst_n) begin
      f_cnt <= 2'd0;
    end else begin
      case ({f_in, f_out})
        2'b01: begin f_q0 <= f_q1; f_cnt <= f_cnt - 2'd1; end
        2'b10: begin
          if (f_cnt == 2'd0) f_q0 <= s_data; else f_q1 <= s_data;
          f_cnt <= f_cnt + 2'd1;
        end
        2'b11: begin
          if (f_cnt == 2'd1) f_q0 <= s_data;
          else begin f_q0 <= f_q1; f_q1 <= s_data; end
        end
        default: ;
      endcase
    end
  end

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (!rst_n) f_was_full <= 1'b0;
    else if (skid_valid) f_was_full <= 1'b1;
  end

  always @(*) if (f_past_valid) begin
    assert(f_cnt <= 2'd2);
    assert(m_valid == (f_cnt != 2'd0));
    assert(s_ready == (f_cnt != 2'd2));
    assert(!skid_valid || m_valid);
    if (f_cnt != 2'd0) assert(m_data == f_q0);
    if (f_cnt == 2'd2) assert(skid_data == f_q1);
  end

  // Hold: a stalled beat stays offered with the same data.
  always @(posedge clk) if (f_past_valid && $past(rst_n) && $past(m_valid && !m_ready)) begin
    assert(m_valid);
    assert(m_data == $past(m_data));
  end

  always @(posedge clk) if (f_past_valid && rst_n && $past(rst_n)) begin
    cover(m_valid && !m_ready);                    // stall
    cover(skid_valid);                             // full slice
    cover(f_was_full && !m_valid);                 // drain after full
    cover($past(f_in && f_out) && f_in && f_out);  // full throughput
  end
`endif

endmodule
`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: skid_buffer_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns/1ps
// Self-checking testbench for skid_buffer, lanes at WIDTH 8 and WIDTH 1.
module skid_buffer_tb;
  reg        clk = 1'b0;
  reg        rst_n = 1'b0;
  reg        s_valid = 1'b0;
  reg  [7:0] s_data = 8'd0;
  reg        m_ready = 1'b0;

  wire       s_ready8, m_valid8;
  wire [7:0] m_data8;
  wire       s_ready1, m_valid1;
  wire [0:0] m_data1;

  skid_buffer #(.WIDTH(8)) dut8 (
    .clk(clk), .rst_n(rst_n),
    .s_valid(s_valid), .s_ready(s_ready8), .s_data(s_data),
    .m_valid(m_valid8), .m_ready(m_ready), .m_data(m_data8));

  skid_buffer #(.WIDTH(1)) dut1 (
    .clk(clk), .rst_n(rst_n),
    .s_valid(s_valid), .s_ready(s_ready1), .s_data(s_data[0:0]),
    .m_valid(m_valid1), .m_ready(m_ready), .m_data(m_data1));

  always #5 clk = ~clk;

  integer passed = 0;
  integer failed = 0;
  integer cnt = 0;
  reg [7:0] q0 = 8'd0;
  reg [7:0] q1 = 8'd0;
  integer sent = 0;
  integer recv = 0;
  integer seed = 32'h5eed1234;
  integer i;
  reg in_f, out_f;
  reg [7:0] d_cap;
  reg sr8, sr1, mv8, mv1;
  reg [7:0] md8;
  reg md1;
  reg prev_stall = 1'b0;
  reg [7:0] prev_data = 8'd0;
  reg [7:0] count_data = 8'd0;
  reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

  task check;
    input cond;
    input [8*40-1:0] msg;
    begin
      if (cond) passed = passed + 1;
      else begin
        failed = failed + 1;
        $error("check failed at %0t: %0s", $time, msg);
      end
    end
  endtask

  // One cycle: inputs already set after the previous edge.
  task step;
    begin
      #1;
      check(m_valid8 == (cnt > 0), "m_valid8 matches model");
      check(m_valid1 == (cnt > 0), "m_valid1 matches model");
      check(s_ready8 == (cnt < 2), "s_ready8 matches model");
      check(s_ready1 == (cnt < 2), "s_ready1 matches model");
      if (cnt > 0) begin
        check(m_data8 == q0, "m_data8 is oldest beat");
        check(m_data1 == q0[0], "m_data1 is oldest beat");
      end
      if (prev_stall) begin
        check(m_valid8 && m_data8 == prev_data, "hold rule");
      end
      // Outputs must not move with m_ready or s_valid inside a cycle.
      sr8 = s_ready8; sr1 = s_ready1; mv8 = m_valid8; mv1 = m_valid1;
      md8 = m_data8; md1 = m_data1[0];
      m_ready = ~m_ready; s_valid = ~s_valid; s_data = ~s_data;
      #1;
      check(s_ready8 == sr8 && s_ready1 == sr1, "s_ready not combinational");
      check(m_valid8 == mv8 && m_valid1 == mv1, "m_valid not combinational");
      if (mv8) check(m_data8 == md8 && m_data1[0] == md1, "m_data not combinational");
      m_ready = ~m_ready; s_valid = ~s_valid; s_data = ~s_data;
      #1;
      in_f  = s_valid && s_ready8;
      out_f = m_valid8 && m_ready;
      d_cap = s_data;
      prev_stall = rst_n && m_valid8 && !m_ready;
      prev_data  = m_data8;
      @(posedge clk);
      if (!rst_n) begin
        cnt = 0;
        prev_stall = 1'b0;
      end else begin
        if (in_f) sent = sent + 1;
        if (out_f) recv = recv + 1;
        if (out_f && !in_f) begin
          q0 = q1; cnt = cnt - 1;
        end else if (in_f && !out_f) begin
          if (cnt == 0) q0 = d_cap; else q1 = d_cap;
          cnt = cnt + 1;
        end else if (in_f && out_f) begin
          if (cnt == 1) q0 = d_cap;
          else begin q0 = q1; q1 = d_cap; end
        end
      end
      #1;
    end
  endtask

  initial begin
    // Reset: apply for two edges before checking anything.
    rst_n = 1'b0;
    @(posedge clk); @(posedge clk); #1;
    step; step;
    check(s_ready8 && !m_valid8 && s_ready1 && !m_valid1, "reset values");
    rst_n = 1'b1;

    // Latency: one beat, offered only after the accepting edge.
    m_ready = 1'b1; s_valid = 1'b1; s_data = 8'hA5;
    step;
    check(m_valid8 && m_data8 == 8'hA5, "beat offered after edge");
    s_valid = 1'b0;
    step;
    check(!m_valid8 && cnt == 0, "single beat drained");

    // Full throughput, counting data.
    m_ready = 1'b1; s_valid = 1'b1;
    for (i = 0; i < 64; i = i + 1) begin
      s_data = count_data; count_data = count_data + 8'd1;
      step;
      check(in_f, "throughput: beat accepted");
      if (i > 0) check(out_f, "throughput: beat leaves, no bubble");
    end
    s_valid = 1'b0;
    step; step;
    check(cnt == 0 && !m_valid8, "throughput stream drained");

    // Stall with one beat held: a second must be accepted; with two, a third must not.
    m_ready = 1'b0; s_valid = 1'b1; s_data = 8'h11;
    step; check(in_f && cnt == 1, "first beat in");
    s_data = 8'h22;
    step; check(in_f && cnt == 2, "second beat accepted while stalled");
    s_data = 8'h33;
    step; check(!in_f && !s_ready8 && !s_ready1, "third beat refused");
    step; check(!in_f && cnt == 2, "still full");
    // Ready rises: beats out in order, once.
    m_ready = 1'b1;
    step; check(out_f && !in_f && cnt == 1 && s_ready8, "skid moves to output");
    step; check(out_f && in_f, "flow after stall");
    s_valid = 1'b0;
    step; step;
    check(cnt == 0 && !m_valid8, "stall test drained");

    // Random traffic against the model.
    for (i = 0; i < 3000; i = i + 1) begin
      s_valid = ($random(seed) & 3) != 0;
      m_ready = ($random(seed) & 3) != 0;
      if (i > 1500) m_ready = ($random(seed) & 1) != 0;
      s_data  = $random(seed);
      step;
    end
    s_valid = 1'b0; m_ready = 1'b1;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) step;
    check(cnt == 0 && !m_valid8 && !m_valid1, "random traffic drained");
    check(sent == recv, "every beat out exactly once");

    // Reset with beats held.
    m_ready = 1'b0; s_valid = 1'b1; s_data = 8'h5A;
    step; step; step;
    check(cnt == 2, "full before reset");
    rst_n = 1'b0;
    step;
    rst_n = 1'b1; s_valid = 1'b0; m_ready = 1'b1;
    step;
    check(!m_valid8 && !m_valid1 && s_ready8 && s_ready1, "reset drops held beats");
    // Traffic after reset.
    s_valid = 1'b1; s_data = 8'h77;
    step; s_valid = 1'b0; step; step;
    check(cnt == 0, "traffic after reset drains");

    if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
    $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
    $finish;
  end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
